      "writtenOn": "2021-12-08T21:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Google style has been to prefer make_unique/make_shared over `unique_ptr\u003cT\u003e(new TSubclass)`: http://go/totw/126\n\nOf course, we generally don\u0027t hold ourselves to Google style rules, sk_sp isn\u0027t literally a shared_ptr, and sk_make_sp isn\u0027t actually make_shared. I think the rationale and principles in this TOTW are solid and still apply in this case, but I don\u0027t feel strongly. If you do, I can undo those lines.",
      "parentUuid": "71d97230_6b39d828",
      "revId": "f0ceca9ea662773c2bd6d1b039c648221a701691",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
